    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Business Travelers Pre-Ride Inspection</h1>
    <p>The pre-ride inspection is the least glamorous five minutes in a business traveler's Hanoi week and the highest-return ones. The trip runs on a fixed schedule, in work clothes, between appointments that do not move, so a machine fault discovered at the counter costs five minutes while the same fault discovered between meetings costs the afternoon. The inspection is also the rare part of the trip that improves with habit: the first pickup walk-around takes ten minutes, the third takes three, and by the second visit it is muscle memory. This page lays out the business traveler's inspection as a repeatable minute-by-minute routine, on verified prices only and no invented shop policies.</p>
    <p>The page is part of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster, written for business travelers. The verified fleet prices sit on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the deeper mechanical background lives in the <a href="/motorbike-guides/motorbike-maintenance-checklist-hanoi/">maintenance checklist</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Why the inspection minute earns its place</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">Lights, horn and the electrical checks</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Brakes, tyres and the stopping question</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Fuel or charge: the range question</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Storage, mirrors and the ergonomic fit</a></li>
